4 in B_2, which is the standard 2-component (4,2) link, not a knot. The companion pair it is compared to, {T(2,9), T(3,5)}, is genuinely two knots (gcd 1 both), which makes the slip easy to miss. The same issue affects 'the lepton tower T(2,k)', which is a knot only for odd k. (2) THE LEAN PATTERN LOOKS SELF-ASSUMING. The block describes MesonGMORFactorization as 'the substrate factorisation axiom' and then says meson_ratio_via_alpha_shift 'proves the factorisation using the specific indices'. If the class carries the factorisation as a field and the theorem projects it, that is the vacuous self-assuming projection AGENTS.md section 3b-cond item 5 forbids — the class must axiomatise the HYPOTHESES, not the conclusion. Worth checking QOU.BraidKnot.meson_ratio_via_alpha_shift directly. (3) NUMBER SUPPLIED (the block quotes none): at the proton pin, [3]_q [4]_q = 12.50866587 against (m_K/m_pi)^2 = 12.51120685 from PDG m_K+- = 493.677, m_pi+- = 139.57039, i.e. -203.1 ppm. Note this disagrees with the sibling prop:meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert, whose route gives -289.65 ppm on the unsquared ratio (about -579 ppm squared): two derivations of the same observable in one chapter, differing by roughly 3x in residual. Also the .ts has uses: [] while the .md cites prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot, so the dependency edge is missing.","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v02","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v02","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v02","notes":"Proposed: either cite where minimality and uniqueness are proved, or restate as 'the pair 